  "method": [
    "Unit counted: one transcribed sub-item. A 'set' is one board situation (3 sub-items) or one standalone item, so for MSTE sets = items.",
    "Each set was assigned to exactly one taxonomy topic by reading its stem. The legacy bank's own topic field was too coarse to use (8 buckets per subject) and was not relied on. Sets that straddle two topics go to the topic that holds most of their sub-items.",
    "mean_share_percent = the topic's share of the transcribed items in a sitting, averaged over the 7 sittings with equal weight. Ranking uses it so a sitting that was only partly transcribed does not count for less. Ties share a rank; topics with no hits share the last rank.",
    "sittings_seen = how many of the 7 sittings had at least one item in the topic (use for the template field board_frequency).",
    "definition_items = items the legacy app flags as TERMS (concept or definition questions with no computation). They are included in items and sets."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "The legacy bank holds 7 sittings (Apr 2023 to Mar 2026) per subject, not the 12 the roadmap mentions. Frequencies are 'x of 7 sittings'.",
    "Transcription is incomplete for some sittings (see per_sitting.coverage_percent; MSTE Apr 2025 holds 21 of 75 items). Compare mean_share_percent, not raw items, across sittings.",
    "MSTE has 54 items on algebra, geometry, trigonometry, analytic geometry and similar that have no topic in the PRC list, plus 8 others outside the 13 MSTE topics. They sit under 'unmapped' rather than being forced into Calculus. Gemz decided on 2026-11-15 to leave them unmapped; the taxonomy stays at the PRC topics.",
    "Borderline placements: dam and wall overturning and sliding sets count under Engineering Mechanics; a cantilever deflection-by-superposition set counts under Strength of Materials; wide-flange beam stress sets count under Steel; water hammer and jet-trajectory items count under Fluid Flow; concrete mix proportioning counts under Construction Materials Testing; Application of the Governing Codes is mostly embedded in the RC and steel sets, so it shows almost nothing.",
    "Several MSTE and HGE counts are small (1 to 5 items), so a rank difference between neighbours there is not meaningful."
  ],
